course: dictionary
lesson: 11534
title: Putting words in alphabetical order
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Alphabetically means in the order of the letters of the alphabet, from A to Z. It is a word about order, not about meaning. «The class lined up alphabetically» means the children stood in a line by their names, with the A names at the front and the Z names at the back.
explain: To sort words alphabetically, look at the first letter of each word. «Apple» comes before «banana» because A comes before B. If the first letters are the same, look at the second letter: «cat» comes before «cup» because A comes before U.
explain: Libraries, dictionaries and school registers use this order so you can find things quickly. «The books on the shelf are arranged alphabetically by author» means you can find an author's name without searching every book. Computers also sort lists alphabetically.
fact: Alphabetically means in the order of the letters of the alphabet, from A to Z.
fact: To sort words alphabetically, compare the first letter of each word.
fact: If the first letters are the same, compare the second letters, then the third, and so on.
fact: «Arranged alphabetically» means put in order from A to Z.
fact: Dictionaries, school registers and library shelves are often kept in alphabetical order.
exercise: Which word comes first alphabetically: pen, apple or sun? | *apple | pen | sun
exercise: «Sort these alphabetically: cup, cat, cap.» Which order is correct? | cat, cap, cup | cup, cap, cat | *cap, cat, cup
exercise: «The books are arranged alphabetically on the shelf.» How are the books arranged? | By colour | *In A to Z order of their letters | By newest first | By size, smallest first
test: Which word would be first if you sort alphabetically: moon, bird or lamp? | lamp | moon | *bird
test: «Sort these alphabetically: tree, table, tiger.» Which list is in the right order? | tree, table, tiger | tiger, table, tree | *table, tiger, tree | table, tree, tiger
exam: Which list is in correct alphabetical order? | bread, cheese, butter | cheese, butter, bread | butter, bread, cheese | *bread, butter, cheese
